/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]channel-versioned, self-updating CLI.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]8[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]4[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plans:202608/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]muse_provider.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202608/muse_provider.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase-ha[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-ha/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Channel-versioned agent-CLI detection and update[/bold #D7AFFF]              [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]cli_meta[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]cli_meta: teach agent-CLI detection, latest-version resolution, and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]update planning about CLIs distributed by a version channel instead of [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]npm — a JSON-endpoint latest oracle, an exact version comparator, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]env-carrying self-update commands, and the `script` install manager.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]The Muse provider and its JSONL stream parser[/bold #D7AFFF]                 [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]provider[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]provider: add `MuseProvider` and `_subprocess_muse`, register the `muse`[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]entry point, map tiers and the full canonical reasoning-effort [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]vocabulary, deploy skills to Muse's native root, add the doctor setup [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]fallback, and test both against recorded release-keyed fixtures.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]sase agent-cli install[/bold #D7AFFF]                                        [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]cli_install[dim] · [dim][/dim]after cli_meta[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]cli_install: add a confirmed, shell-free `sase agent-cli install` [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]subcommand that fetches a provider-declared installer over HTTPS, shows [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]its digest before running it, and never edits the user's shell rc files.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Usage, tool-call, and model-identity artifacts[/bold #D7AFFF]                [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]artifacts[dim] · [dim][/dim]after provider[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]artifacts: extract tool calls from the Muse event stream, recover token [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]usage from the session log SASE owns via `--session-id`, and record the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]model Muse actually configured.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Model advisories and the Contributor data-sharing guard[/bold #D7AFFF]       [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]advisory[dim] · [dim][/dim]after provider[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]advisory: add a provider-neutral model-advisory hook, surface it in the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]model picker, `%model` completion, and model labels, and add a doctor [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]check that reports when a resolved default routes SASE traffic to an [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]advisory-flagged model.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]ACE styling and provider badges[/bold #D7AFFF]                               [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]polish[dim] · [dim][/dim]after provider[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]polish: give Muse a Meta-blue provider palette, an emoji badge, and a [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]family color so agent rows, model labels, and integrations render it as [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]a 